<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/3rd-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Cannae</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">216 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a> · Also known as Cannae · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-punic-war">Second Punic War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Cannae was fought in 216 BCE in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-punic-war">Second Punic War</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a>'s Carthaginian army encircled and destroyed a much larger Roman army. Although it is one of the most famous tactical victories in history, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> refused to surrender and eventually defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punic-empire">Punic Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-cannae.jpg" alt="Battle of Cannae" width="320" height="224" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Trumbull · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Death_of_Paulus_Aemilius_at_the_Battle_of_Cannae_(Yale_University_Art_Gallery_scan).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
